WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.440
Your coding agent spent an hour on a bug.

2
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.892
Then the context was compacted.

3
00:00:06.992 --> 00:00:08.995
Now it starts from zero.

4
00:00:11.345 --> 00:00:13.742
It reads the same files again.

5
00:00:13.842 --> 00:00:16.264
It tries the fix that already failed.

6
00:00:18.445 --> 00:00:21.563
Agentpack keeps the task state in your repo.

7
00:00:21.663 --> 00:00:27.416
Not the chat: the goal, the decisions, the dead ends, the evidence, and the next step.

8
00:00:30.345 --> 00:00:34.169
While the agent works, it records only what is worth keeping.

9
00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:48.956
Next day. New session. Empty context.

10
00:00:49.056 --> 00:00:52.591
One call, and the agent knows where the task stands.

11
00:00:58.345 --> 00:01:03.901
Any MCP client can continue: Claude Code, Codex, or Cursor.

12
00:01:05.345 --> 00:01:07.636
Plain files. No cloud.

13
00:01:07.736 --> 00:01:10.828
A gate that warns when the agent leaves its task.

14
00:01:13.145 --> 00:01:17.476
Three commands, and your next session starts where the last one stopped.
